From 2ec0065360f680b6817577ad06fa14b77beb544e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:13:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Security hardening, LinkedIn login, repo cleanup

- Only jobseeker/recruiter/company/college can be chosen at sign-up (email and
  social); fixes admin role self-assignment via /auth/google?role=admin
- complete-social-profile now requires the signed-in token (no userId in body)
- Remove 'fallback_secret'; server refuses to start without a 32+ char JWT_SECRET;
  token lifetime 30d (JWT_EXPIRES_IN); blocked users are refused immediately
- OTP: crypto.randomInt, 5-attempt limit, constant-time compare; emails coerced
  to strings (NoSQL operator injection); generic forgot-password response;
  OTPs no longer logged; errors no longer return stack traces
- Rate limiting on auth routes (dependency-free limiter)
- Sockets require a valid JWT and membership for rooms/groups; no client-driven
  group broadcast
- No default admin account; first admin comes from ADMIN_EMAIL/ADMIN_PASSWORD
- Replace GitHub login with LinkedIn (OpenID Connect); add Google/LinkedIn buttons
- Fix social login always issuing a jobseeker token (role was not populated)
- Untrack server/uploads and client/.env; remove genToken.js and build log
- Optional PROTECT_DOCUMENT_UPLOADS flag for /uploads documents
- Add tests, .env.example files, README and docs

